      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:28 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2011-11-199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6a630a9eb5e9cbc45b6a2c431125c177d733b6b8a734bb350d3c0a229ec519f8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a630a9eb5e9-0000-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "BEAU B. BRINDLEY, ESQ., Chicago, Illinois; for Petitioner. ANTHONY A. YANG, ESQ., Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; for Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2011-11-199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6a630a9eb5e9cbc45b6a2c431125c177d733b6b8a734bb350d3c0a229ec519f8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a630a9eb5e9-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "When determining whether an error affects substantial rights pursuant to the harmless-error statute, courts should first begin the analysis with the error itself, consider it in the context of the entire record, determine what potential impact it may have, and then ask the question: Can the government prove to the requisite degree of certitude -- in this case, fair assurance -- that the error did not substantially impact the verdict of the jury that heard the case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2011-11-199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6a630a9eb5e9cbc45b6a2c431125c177d733b6b8a734bb350d3c0a229ec519f8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a630a9eb5e9-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Could you tell me what the error actually was? I see -- and you can add another -- three potential things about these calls or three potential errors: One, that they proved as a matter of fact that she was biased."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2011-11-199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6a630a9eb5e9cbc45b6a2c431125c177d733b6b8a734bb350d3c0a229ec519f8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a630a9eb5e9-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is it correct that the difference between your position and the Government's position is that the Government says the focus should be on a rational jury, and you say the focus should be on this particular jury?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2011-11-199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6a630a9eb5e9cbc45b6a2c431125c177d733b6b8a734bb350d3c0a229ec519f8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a630a9eb5e9-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, let me -- let me read you two sentences and tell me whether you think there's a difference between them."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2011-11-199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6a630a9eb5e9cbc45b6a2c431125c177d733b6b8a734bb350d3c0a229ec519f8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a630a9eb5e9-0000-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What would you point at in the majority opinion below that suggests that they did an analysis that didn't look at the error and its possible prejudicial effect?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2011-11-199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6a630a9eb5e9cbc45b6a2c431125c177d733b6b8a734bb350d3c0a229ec519f8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a630a9eb5e9-0000-0010",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "At that moment your client's lawyer, who they call \"Beau\" -- is that right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2011-11-199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6a630a9eb5e9cbc45b6a2c431125c177d733b6b8a734bb350d3c0a229ec519f8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a630a9eb5e9-0000-0011",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 15,
        "start": 15
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "trying to do is you want Perez to plead guilty. Is that the fair thrust of this?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2011-11-199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6a630a9eb5e9cbc45b6a2c431125c177d733b6b8a734bb350d3c0a229ec519f8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a630a9eb5e9-0000-0012",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 17,
        "start": 17
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Okay. So, would it satisfy you in your opinion if we said: We aren't finding your opinion totally clear."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2011-11-199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6a630a9eb5e9cbc45b6a2c431125c177d733b6b8a734bb350d3c0a229ec519f8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a630a9eb5e9-0000-0013",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "that verdict the -- whether without that error, the verdict would be the same."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2011-11-199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6a630a9eb5e9cbc45b6a2c431125c177d733b6b8a734bb350d3c0a229ec519f8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a630a9eb5e9-0000-0014",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Are you saying that it doesn't matter that the verdict would have been the same by this jury if the error had not been made?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2011-11-199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6a630a9eb5e9cbc45b6a2c431125c177d733b6b8a734bb350d3c0a229ec519f8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a630a9eb5e9-0000-0015",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, then, what is harmless error?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2011-11-199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6a630a9eb5e9cbc45b6a2c431125c177d733b6b8a734bb350d3c0a229ec519f8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a630a9eb5e9-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Could we get a little more practical here? I think I understood your basic argument, which is: My defense was by this one woman, the wife of one of the codefendants. She tells a story, and if the jury had believed her story they would have acquitted your client."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2011-11-199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6a630a9eb5e9cbc45b6a2c431125c177d733b6b8a734bb350d3c0a229ec519f8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a630a9eb5e9-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Are you -- are you taking the position in this case that a reviewing court, under no circumstance, could conclude that this error was harmless? Or are you taking the position in this case that the court here, the Seventh Circuit, I think, committed review error and we should send it back for them to do it the right way?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Brindley",
      "case_id": "2011-11-199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6a630a9eb5e9cbc45b6a2c431125c177d733b6b8a734bb350d3c0a229ec519f8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a630a9eb5e9-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BRINDLEY: Yes. Yes, Your Honor. I agree with that. The problem is the question asked by the majority strips out the error and it also focuses on the reasonable jury rather than this jury."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2011-11-199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6a630a9eb5e9cbc45b6a2c431125c177d733b6b8a734bb350d3c0a229ec519f8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a630a9eb5e9-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Can you say that this jury was uninfluenced by that error?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2011-11-199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6a630a9eb5e9cbc45b6a2c431125c177d733b6b8a734bb350d3c0a229ec519f8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a630a9eb5e9-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Isn't that -- don't we take into account that the government itself thought this was very important?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2011-11-199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6a630a9eb5e9cbc45b6a2c431125c177d733b6b8a734bb350d3c0a229ec519f8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a630a9eb5e9-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Yang, why does any of this have to do with her credibility? Did the dissent say that the way this affected the jury was that it rendered her less credible?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2011-11-199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6a630a9eb5e9cbc45b6a2c431125c177d733b6b8a734bb350d3c0a229ec519f8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a630a9eb5e9-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Suppose -- suppose the judge concludes that both this jury that I had and some hypothetical rational jury would have been so focused on this evidence that that's all they would have looked at, but if they had looked at 1 through 9, the admissible evidence, they would still have found guilt."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2011-11-199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6a630a9eb5e9cbc45b6a2c431125c177d733b6b8a734bb350d3c0a229ec519f8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a630a9eb5e9-0002-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The government has to show, as -- this is the formulation in Neder and which the Court has said in Neder is the same thing that applied in erroneous admissions or exclusions of evidence, that a rational jury would have found the defendant guilty absent the error, and that involves the three core elements we explained in our brief."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2011-11-199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6a630a9eb5e9cbc45b6a2c431125c177d733b6b8a734bb350d3c0a229ec519f8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a630a9eb5e9-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Did the panel majority in -- did the panel majority in this case say anything that differs from what this Court has said about harmless error? If we were to reverse, what would we point to in the panel majority's opinion that was erroneous?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2011-11-199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6a630a9eb5e9cbc45b6a2c431125c177d733b6b8a734bb350d3c0a229ec519f8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a630a9eb5e9-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Hasn't this Court said exactly what Seventh Circuit said there? In other cases?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2011-11-199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6a630a9eb5e9cbc45b6a2c431125c177d733b6b8a734bb350d3c0a229ec519f8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a630a9eb5e9-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: You want us to say -- you want us to say we're reversing you, Seventh Circuit panel, because you said what we have said in prior cases, but we were wrong?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2011-11-199",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "6a630a9eb5e9cbc45b6a2c431125c177d733b6b8a734bb350d3c0a229ec519f8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a630a9eb5e9-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BRINDLEY: I think the reason to reverse them is because that formulation has proven to lead to the wrong analysis, in all of these lower courts, this guilt-based approach; and it is not the law of Kotteakos. This Court has never overruled Kotteakos."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2011-11-199",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6a630a9eb5e9cbc45b6a2c431125c177d733b6b8a734bb350d3c0a229ec519f8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6a630a9eb5e9-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted."
    },
    {
